0 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186532592 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186532390 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186532592 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186532592 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186532592 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186532082 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186532592 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "d2718901-61ad-591c-ba8b-c2899ee3b35f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186532620 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186532592 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186532620 #edb/ref 1069 "q-162815" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186532620 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186532620 #edb/ref 1071 "Suppose we would like to find the minimum of the function $f(x,y,z)=xy-zy$ on the intersection of the surfaces $y+z=1$ and ${x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}=1$ using the method of Lagrange multipliers. Then, the corresponding Lagrange multipliers $\\lambda $ and $\\mu $ satisfy the following system: \n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}⟨y,\\,\\bbox[2pt,border:1pt solid black]{\\phantom{AA}},\\,-y⟩=\\lambda ⟨0,\\,1,\\,\\bbox[2pt,border:1pt solid black]{\\phantom{AA}}\\,⟩+\\mu ⟨2x,\\,2y,\\,\\bbox[2pt,border:1pt solid black]{\\phantom{AA}}\\,⟩ \\\\ y+z=1 \\\\ {x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFrom left to right, what are the missing parts of the expressions?" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186532620 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "01a5e642-9803-5a1b-8846-85c812cf1513" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186532620 #edb/ref 1074 "We need to find the minimum value of \n\n$$\nf(x,y,z)=xy-zy\n$$\n\n \n\nsubject to the constraints \n\n$$\ng(x,y,z)=y+z=1,\\,h(x,y,z)={x}^{2}+{y}^{2}+{z}^{2}=1.\n$$\n\nTherefore, by the method of Lagrange multipliers, we must solve the following system:\n\n$$\n\\{\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y,z)=\\lambda ∇g(x,y,z)+\\mu ∇h(x,y,z) \\\\ g(x,y,z)=1 \\\\ h(x,y,z)=1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nWe now expand the first equation of the system:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}∇f(x,y,z) & =\\lambda ∇g(x,y,z)+\\mu ∇h(x,y,z) \\\\ ⟨{f}_{x},{f}_{y},{f}_{z}⟩ & =\\lambda ⟨{g}_{x},{g}_{y},{g}_{z}⟩+\\mu ⟨{h}_{x},{h}_{y},{h}_{z}⟩ \\\\ ⟨y,\\,x-z,\\,-y⟩ & =\\lambda ⟨0,\\,1,\\,1⟩+\\mu ⟨2x,\\,2y,\\,2z⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
